  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria Peace Initiative III (SPI III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The Action aims at providing a flexible and quickly responding instrument to continue to capitalise on and support emergent political and peacebuilding opportunities in Syria.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Specific Objectives&lt;/strong&gt; (SO, outcomes) of the Action are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Political Process Support&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;SO1 &amp;nbsp;The political process is supported, and related opposition actors are enabled to negotiate effectively and to leverage their position in the peace process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Civil Society Support&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;SO2&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The peace process is made more inclusive and is strengthened by peacebuilding efforts of civil society actors at all levels.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Research and Analysis&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;SO3&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Access to information and context- and conflict-sensitive analysis on Syrian and regional developments for the political steering of the initiative is ensured.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
